<DocsLayout
  title="Use Kvendra from Codex CLI — Kvendra developer docs"
  description="Connect Codex CLI to the same Kvendra knowledge base you use from Claude Code: three lines of config, the usual Kvendra sign-in and a short AGENTS.md boot file."
>
  <span class="kvd-kicker">Guide</span>
  <h1>Use Kvendra from Codex CLI</h1>
  <p>
    Kvendra is a hosted knowledge base that your agents reach over MCP. It works
    with Claude Code and Codex CLI. This page connects Codex CLI to the same
    knowledge base you use from Claude Code.
  </p>

  <h2>You need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A Kvendra account with Pro (the 15-day trial works).</li>
    <li>Codex CLI, signed in with your own OpenAI account (<code>codex login</code>).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>1. Add Kvendra to Codex</h2>
  <p>In <code>~/.codex/config.toml</code>:</p>
  <pre class="kvd-codex__toml"><code>{TOML}</code></pre>

  <h2>2. Sign in to Kvendra</h2>
  <p>
    Run <code>codex mcp login kvendra-cloud</code>. Your browser opens the Kvendra
    sign-in. When it finishes, <code>codex mcp list</code> shows
    <code>kvendra-cloud</code> as enabled with OAuth. No token to copy or paste.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Add a boot file</h2>
  <p>
    Put an <code>AGENTS.md</code> in your project root: a short file that tells
    Codex where the project’s memory lives and how to start each session.
  </p>
  <pre class="kvd-codex__agents"><code>{AGENTS}</code></pre>

  <h2>4. Start a session</h2>
  <p>
    Ask Codex to start the session. It calls <code>help</code> with the bootstrap
    topic, loads your project, roadmaps, recent releases and open issues, and
    works from there. A decision it records lands in the same knowledge base
    Claude Code reads.
  </p>

  <h2>Approvals</h2>
  <p>
    In the interactive Codex app you approve each Kvendra call. For
    non-interactive runs (<code>codex exec</code>), add
    <code>default_tools_approval_mode = "approve"</code> to the server block;
    without it every Kvendra call stops for approval.
  </p>

  <h2>What is different from Claude Code</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Same: every knowledge-base tool (entities, transactions, search, files,
      messages) and the boot sequence.
    </li>
    <li>
      Native only in Claude Code: skills such as <code>/kvendra</code> and
      <code>/new-feature</code>, hooks, and subagent pipelines. In Codex, the
      AGENTS.md and the procedures stored in your knowledge base guide the agent
      instead. Code work can still run through the cloud pipeline: an issue
      marked ready runs whichever agent wrote it.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Safety</h2>
  <p>
    Claude Code with the Kvendra plugin has a protection hook that blocks unsafe
    operations. Codex does not. If Codex has shell access, keep it in a
    read-only sandbox for now.
  </p>

  <h2>Tested with</h2>
  <p>
    Codex CLI 0.167.2 and the hosted Kvendra MCP, on 2026-11-12. The full
    experiment: <a href="/labs/codex-cli/">Lab 01</a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
